# Vercel reads this INSTEAD of .gitignore when deciding what to upload.
#
# That is the whole reason this file exists. `frontend/public/data/` is gitignored so the
# repository can be public without carrying the dataset, but the deployed site still has to
# serve it. Without this file the CLI would fall back to .gitignore and upload a site with
# no data.
#
# So: never add frontend/public/data/ here.

node_modules
.next
screenshots
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.vercel
